# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile actually COPYs: pom.xml, src/ and
# cosyfs/. Everything else only inflates the context that has to be shipped to the
# builder — and, more importantly, invalidates the build cache: BuildKit hashes the
# whole context for `COPY . .`-style layers, so a stray edit to docs/ or a local
# `target/` rebuild would drop the cached rust and maven layers the PR systemtest gate
# depends on for a tolerable turnaround.
#
# Expect no speedup on a fresh CI checkout (there is no target/ or .idea/ there); this
# matters for local `docker build` and for cache stability.

# Build output
target/
cosyfs/target/

# VCS and IDE
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.mvn

# Docs and non-build assets
docs/
dummy/
infrastructure/
scripts/
*.md
LICENSE

# Local config — must never reach an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# CI definitions
.github/
